{"shortDescription":"Cash basis bids for soybeans and corn were unchanged in the U.S. Midwest on Friday after a wild week in which soaring Chicago Board of Trade futures prompted farmers to sell some of their remaining 2025 and expected 2026 harvests, merchandisers said.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in c…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Cash basis bids for soybeans and corn were unchanged in the U.S. Midwest on Friday after a wild week in which soaring Chicago Board of Trade futures prompted farmers to sell some of their remaining 2025 and expected 2026 harvests, merchandisers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Basis moves for both crops were mixed this week. Benchmark CBOT corn futures ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZC1!","text":"CBOT:ZC1!"}}," hit a three-year high on Friday and soybean futures ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"CBOT:ZS1!","text":"CBOT:ZS1!"}}," touched a 2-1/2-year high, encouraging scattered grain sales by producers."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["But cash sales were tempered by farmers' uncertainty about their own yield prospects, and some growers were content to hold out for even higher prices, brokers said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["A few soybean processors raised their spot soybean basis this week as they worked to secure enough old-crop soybeans to cover their needs until the new-crop harvest begins this autumn. The posted basis for spot soybeans at Sioux City, Iowa, on Thursday reached $1 a bushel over CBOT November futures."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Crush margins for soy processors have fallen from historic highs set in June but remain profitable, with the CBOT December-November \"board crush\" (SMSIZ26-BOZ26-SX26), one indication of soy processors' profit margins, holding well over $2 a bushel."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","childr